From e387d3a9fa7f989370beaf5a1c791a2219d2826a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: EscapeA <escapea@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 09:03:58 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(security): key login throttling on the real client
 address

Behind a reverse proxy (Cloudflare Tunnel, nginx) ctx.ip is always the proxy
socket, so every visitor shared one throttle bucket: ten anonymous failed
logins locked the whole installation for an hour, and clearing it required an
already-authenticated request.

- add resolveClientIp: honours cf-connecting-ip / x-real-ip / last x-forwarded-for
  hop only when the TCP peer is a trusted proxy (default: loopback), so a LAN or
  Tailnet client cannot spoof its own address
- exempt loopback from the global ceiling so an operator can always reach the
  unlock endpoint
- stop publishing build details, the agent-bridge pid and host facts from
  /health and /api/devices/link-info to unauthenticated callers
- require auth for speech synthesis; keep the MCU prompt-tone route public
- stop hermes-web-ui client mode from forcing CORS_ORIGINS=*
